From 5033e6d70a5314eb9d934c07c4521375bcf59d48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 20:36:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(eligibility): qualify the project before selling
 anything
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The free calculator computed NPV for whatever you typed and handed over a PDF
regardless of whether the project could ever proceed. It qualified nobody — a
serious buyer with a real constellation got the same answer as someone dragging
sliders, and Eligibility Checks were being sold into projects that were never
eligible.

This turns the wedge into a filter.

- shared/eligibility.ts (new): deterministic, rule-based engine returning
  ELIGIBLE | LIKELY_ELIGIBLE | REQUIRES_REVIEW | NOT_ELIGIBLE |
  INSUFFICIENT_DATA with findings. No model, no inference, no invented facts.
- Precedence is explicit: a KNOWN blocker outranks a missing fact. Reporting
  "incomplete" when we can already see it cannot work would be dodging the
  answer.
- It never declares legal compliance. It reports economic and structural
  preconditions and says so in those words; a test sweeps all four verdict
  paths for compliance language and for any § character.
- Unknown is a first-class state. Four optional questions (owner constellation,
  spatial scope, generation status, metering); unanswered ones are reported as
  NAMED gaps with the reason each matters, instead of defaulting to the answer
  that flatters the project. That named gap is the honest argument for the paid
  Eligibility Check.
- After every result: feasibility, value driver, main risk, missing data, next
  paid step, effort band. Never "Contact us" — the step is named with a reason
  specific to the verdict, and it routes eligibility → structuring → mandate on
  actual complexity. A disqualified constellation gets NO paid step at all;
  selling into a known blocker is selling a failure.
- Effort is a scope band (gering/mittel/hoch), never a duration — the AGB still
  states no turnaround.
- The paid step reuses PILOT_OFFER_FULFILLMENT, so the calculator, the PDF and
  the post-payment confirmation ask for exactly the same intake data.
- EligibilityPanel sits between the numbers and the lead capture, so nobody
  reaches the PDF without seeing the verdict. Facts are owned by the calculator,
  not the panel, so the downloaded PDF carries the same verdict the visitor read.
- The report's closing block is now that verdict plus the concrete next step and
  its intake checklist, replacing the generic "bezahlte Pilotaufnahme" CTA.

Three defects found by rendering the output rather than trusting the types:
- effortBand read an UNANSWERED scope question as "not single building" and
  reported "hoch" to every visitor who answered nothing. Absence is uncertainty,
  not complexity.
- CTA prose overflowed the right edge of the green panel.
- The provenance section forced an unconditional page break, leaving page 2 half
  empty; it now starts inline when there is room and lets autoTable flow.

Evidence: pnpm check clean, 134/134 vitest (33 new eligibility + 5 new PDF
assertions against the rendered document), pnpm build clean, smoke 16/16.

